<%# THE EDIT PAGE'S two browser-only controls.

    Both were added on the operator's call (2026-08-15) and both are invisible to
    every server-side tier for the usual reason: the markup is identical whether
    the browser program works or is dead.

      1. THE AVATAR OVERLAY. The 28px pencil badge is gone; the picture is the
         button, and hovering the card fades a "Change photo" label over it.
         A String assertion sees the label on every render — it is always in the
         document — and can say nothing about whether it is ever VISIBLE, because
         that is a computed opacity set by a CSS hover rule. It also cannot say
         whether clicking actually reaches the file picker.

      2. THE BIRTHDAY CALENDAR. Its popover is `position: fixed`, and the two
         positioning modes are INDISTINGUISHABLE until the page scrolls — at
         scroll 0 they land in the same place. The defect is a geometry fact:
         the element renders, has correct markup, and is simply in the wrong
         place. Only a browser can tell them apart, and only after scrolling.
         This page reproduces the edit page's overflow-hidden container so the
         specs run against the real shape.

    LOCALS ONLY, per test/lib/e2e_lane_contract_test.rb: this page may set a
    partial's locals and nothing else. Every control below comes from an ENGINE
    partial rendered BY NAME.
%>
<div x-data="studioProfileForm(<%= { first_name: @user.first_name, last_name: @user.last_name, email: @user.email, birthday: "" }.to_json %>)">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto py-8">
    <%# imageUploadHost is defined inside this partial, and editable_identity's
        x-data calls it. The cropper library it also pulls in comes from a CDN,
        which the lane answers with an empty 200 (see blockOffsiteRequests) — so
        the CROPPING is not under test here, only that clicking the avatar
        reaches the picker.

        (The guard in e2e_lane_contract_test.rb refuses the literal opening tag
        of a browser program anywhere in a lab page, comments included, and that
        bluntness is deliberate: an ERB comment ends at its FIRST `%>`, so a
        leaked one turns its own prose into a phantom element. That is exactly
        how the at-time defect shipped.) %>
    <%= render "studio/cropper_assets" %>

    <%= render "studio/profiles/editable_identity", user: @user %>

    <form x-ref="form" data-studio-lab-form>
      <%# THE CLIPPING CONTAINER, reproduced deliberately. `card p-0
          overflow-hidden` is what edit.html.erb wraps its rows in. A lab page
          rendering the field bare would be a different shape from the real page,
          and the popover's placement would be tested against conditions no
          consumer ever renders. %>
      <div class="card p-0 overflow-hidden">
        <section class="p-6" data-profile-section="birthday">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-heading mb-4">Birthday</h2>
          <%= render "studio/profiles/birthday_fields", user: @user %>
        </section>
      </div>
    </form>

    <%# Runway, so there is somewhere to scroll when the popover has to flip. %>
    <div data-studio-lab-spacer style="height: 120vh;"></div>
  </div>

  <%= render "studio/profiles/save_bar" %>
</div>

<%= render "studio/profiles/form_script" %>
